From d0ef0ba402dc6e2b7a3c00bb56c22859b116f475 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Gon=C3=A7alves?= <bigbruno@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:28:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] icontheme: Look up icons in icon-theme.cache instead of
 listing them

When a theme directory has an up-to-date icon-theme.cache, loading the
theme listed every icon of every theme directory from the cache into
per-size hash tables and interned every name. With a large theme (76
directories, 20000 names) that costs 50 ms at the first lookup of every
process and 3.5 MiB of heap.

Keep the cache mapped and answer lookups from its hash table, as GTK 3
did. Directories without a cache are still listed when the theme loads.
Cached and listed directories of a size keep their order, so the first
directory that has an icon still wins. gtk_icon_theme_get_icon_names()
lists the cached directories when it is called.

icontheme also runs on copies of the test themes that have an
icon-theme.cache, one of which lists an icon that is not on disk.
